{
  "dom_id": "step-q56537",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$\\frac{3}{8}\\times 2=$",
  "worked_solution": "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 2}{8}=\\frac{6}{8}\n$$\n\nWe then reduce this fraction to its lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{8}=\\frac{6÷2}{8÷2}=\\frac{3}{4}\n$$",
